# =============================================================================
# Unhoard .gitignore
# Sections: (1) private files that must never be published, (2) secrets,
# (3) user data the app produces, (4) build output and tooling noise.
# When in doubt, keep a file out of git: a leaked file cannot be unpublished.
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. Private working files (never public) ---------------------------------
# CLAUDE.md is the maintainer's private working agreement with Claude Code.
# The public equivalent for contributors and AI agents is AGENTS.md.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
**/CLAUDE.md
.claude/
# Anything personal: notes, drafts, handoffs, design explorations.
private/
*.private.*
*.local.*
*.local
# Editor and OS clutter that can contain personal paths.
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.code-workspace
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- 2. Secrets and signing material -----------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.snk
*.keystore
*.jks
secrets/
*.secret
*.secrets
client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json

# --- 3. Data the app produces (may contain personal file paths) --------------
# Scan exports, snapshots, logs and quarantine manifests describe a real disk.
# Folder patterns are anchored to the repo root (leading /) so they never hide
# source folders with the same name, such as src/quarantine/.
*.scan.json
*.scan.csv
/scan-exports/
/scan-snapshots/
/quarantine/
Unhoard Quarantine/
*.unhoard-manifest.json
/logs/
*.log
# Test media is always generated by the test suite, never real photos.
tests/fixtures/generated/
test-output/
perf/results/
dist-fake/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# --- 4. Build output and tooling ---------------------------------------------
# Rust
target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Node / frontend
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
# Python (docs check script)
__pycache__/
# Tauri bundles and generated schemas
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/schemas/
# Downloaded AI models (large, fetched on demand)
/models/
*.gguf
*.onnx
